WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.967 --> 00:00:02.901
A president accused of a crime

00:00:02.901 --> 00:00:05.705
is insisting we need
a border wall to prevent crime.

00:00:05.705 --> 00:00:09.075
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:09.075 --> 00:00:12.378
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:12.378 --> 00:00:15.482
There's a phrase politicians
on both sides of the aisle

00:00:15.482 --> 00:00:16.849
have been using for decades,

00:00:16.849 --> 00:00:18.784
and that is
"we are a nation of laws,"

00:00:18.784 --> 00:00:21.054
but in particular,
Republicans and President Trump

00:00:21.054 --> 00:00:23.756
have used it in recent years
to justify policies

00:00:23.756 --> 00:00:25.658
that target groups
they want to punish

00:00:25.658 --> 00:00:28.361
like their political opponents
or undocumented immigrants.

00:00:28.361 --> 00:00:31.497
-We are a nation of laws, and
we need to uphold those laws.

00:00:31.497 --> 00:00:34.266
-You have to understand
we're a nation of laws.

00:00:34.266 --> 00:00:35.668
Do you respect that?

00:00:35.668 --> 00:00:38.004
-Under the Trump administration,

00:00:38.004 --> 00:00:40.940
America is once more
a nation of laws.

00:00:40.940 --> 00:00:42.841
-Of course,
the more we learn about Trump,

00:00:42.841 --> 00:00:44.911
the more I think he means that
as a complaint.

00:00:44.911 --> 00:00:46.579
"They won't let me do anything
around here.

00:00:46.579 --> 00:00:48.615
It's like we're
a nation of laws."

00:00:48.615 --> 00:00:50.783
[ Laughter ]

00:00:50.783 --> 00:00:54.087
And Trump has even used
the "nation of laws" line

00:00:54.087 --> 00:00:57.257
when asked specifically
about vulnerable people

00:00:57.257 --> 00:00:58.691
fleeing poverty and violence

00:00:58.691 --> 00:01:00.659
and seeking asylum
here in the U.S.,

00:01:00.659 --> 00:01:02.061
which is a legal right

00:01:02.061 --> 00:01:04.296
under both U.S.
and international law.

00:01:04.296 --> 00:01:06.732
-The caravan has arrived
at the U.S. border.

00:01:06.732 --> 00:01:08.868
-We've been watching it.
We've been watching it.

00:01:08.868 --> 00:01:12.171
-And I'm just wondering in your
opinion or in your estimation,

00:01:12.171 --> 00:01:14.874
what percentage of those people
do you believe

00:01:14.874 --> 00:01:17.410
are deserving of asylum
in the U.S.?

00:01:17.410 --> 00:01:19.279
-Well, I won't
get into percentages,

00:01:19.279 --> 00:01:21.280
but we are a nation of laws.

00:01:21.280 --> 00:01:24.149
-I love when Trump says,
"I won't get into percentages,"

00:01:24.149 --> 00:01:25.518
because what he really means is

00:01:25.518 --> 00:01:28.554
"I don't understand
percentages."

00:01:28.554 --> 00:01:31.591
If you asked him
how much fat is in 2% milk,

00:01:31.591 --> 00:01:33.259
he'd be up all night
at a chalkboard

00:01:33.259 --> 00:01:36.128
doing math like in
"Good Will Hunting."

00:01:36.128 --> 00:01:39.999
And when you asked him what
the answer was, he'd say,

00:01:39.999 --> 00:01:43.169
"All I know is I ate the chalk.

00:01:43.169 --> 00:01:46.439
How do you like them apples?!"

00:01:46.439 --> 00:01:48.942
[ Laughter ]

00:01:50.743 --> 00:01:52.945
But it's especially infuriating
to watch Trump

00:01:52.945 --> 00:01:55.715
pretend to care about the law
when his own Justice Department

00:01:55.715 --> 00:01:57.116
just accused him of a crime

00:01:57.116 --> 00:01:59.318
for paying hush money
to cover up affairs.

00:01:59.318 --> 00:02:01.153
Today the man
who made those payments,

00:02:01.153 --> 00:02:02.588
Trump's ex-fixer Michael Cohen,

00:02:02.588 --> 00:02:04.490
was sentenced
to three years in jail.

00:02:04.490 --> 00:02:06.692
And during the hearing,
Cohen told the court

00:02:06.692 --> 00:02:09.194
in no uncertain terms
that he committed those crimes

00:02:09.194 --> 00:02:10.763
at the direction
of Donald Trump.

00:02:10.763 --> 00:02:13.166
-The former Trump attorney
and fixer Michael Cohen

00:02:13.166 --> 00:02:16.168
speaking moments ago inside
a New York federal courtroom.

00:02:16.168 --> 00:02:17.803
Cohen now says he accepts

00:02:17.803 --> 00:02:20.306
"full responsibility"
for his crimes,

00:02:20.306 --> 00:02:21.640
the one he committed on his own

00:02:21.640 --> 00:02:23.242
and the ones
he and prosecutors say

00:02:23.242 --> 00:02:25.044
he committed at the direction

00:02:25.044 --> 00:02:27.247
of the President
of the United States.

00:02:27.247 --> 00:02:30.015
-Federal prosecutors working
for the Department of Justice

00:02:30.015 --> 00:02:33.085
now claiming
that then-candidate Trump

00:02:33.085 --> 00:02:36.221
directed illegal hush money
to two women

00:02:36.221 --> 00:02:38.524
during the 2016 campaign.

00:02:38.524 --> 00:02:40.960
-For the first time,
you have federal prosecutors

00:02:40.960 --> 00:02:42.528
essentially saying

00:02:42.528 --> 00:02:45.297
that Donald Trump
committed a felony.

00:02:45.297 --> 00:02:47.700
-Damn. Forget running
for re-election.

00:02:47.700 --> 00:02:50.770
In two years, Trump might be
running from the feds.

00:02:50.770 --> 00:02:53.173
The FBI is going to
bust into a cabin in Montana

00:02:53.173 --> 00:02:55.141
and find Trump
with a Unabomber beard

00:02:55.141 --> 00:02:58.211
surrounded by
Burger King wrappers.

00:02:58.211 --> 00:03:01.714
"Wait. Wait. How --
How did you find me?"

00:03:01.714 --> 00:03:04.851
"Um, you put your name
on the cabin."

00:03:04.851 --> 00:03:07.119
[ Laughter ]

00:03:07.119 --> 00:03:08.788
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:08.788 --> 00:03:12.625
"Ohh. Ohh!"

00:03:12.625 --> 00:03:14.360
Republicans have spent years
insisting

00:03:14.360 --> 00:03:16.862
that we can't admit immigrants
fleeing poverty and violence

00:03:16.862 --> 00:03:18.097
because we're a nation of laws,

00:03:18.097 --> 00:03:19.966
and yet now that the actual
Justice Department

00:03:19.966 --> 00:03:21.868
has accused the President
of the United States

00:03:21.868 --> 00:03:23.770
of committing a crime,
suddenly Republicans

00:03:23.770 --> 00:03:26.338
are getting very squishy on that
whole "nation of laws" thing.

00:03:26.338 --> 00:03:29.242
And the best example of that
is Utah Senator Orrin Hatch,

00:03:29.242 --> 00:03:31.243
who tried to claim
the Cohen charges

00:03:31.243 --> 00:03:34.246
were part of a Democratic
conspiracy to take down Trump.

00:03:34.246 --> 00:03:37.550
-The Democrats will do anything
to hurt this president.

00:03:37.550 --> 00:03:38.751
Anything.

00:03:38.751 --> 00:03:40.186
-But it's not the Democrats.

00:03:40.186 --> 00:03:42.321
It's the Southern District
of New York, the U.S. Attorney.

00:03:42.321 --> 00:03:44.790
I mean, that's what's making
this allegation.

00:03:44.790 --> 00:03:47.794
-Okay, but I don't care.

00:03:47.794 --> 00:03:52.464
-I love how he starts out
with one argument

00:03:52.464 --> 00:03:54.867
and then, when that argument
is rebutted,

00:03:54.867 --> 00:03:57.036
just says, "I don't care."

00:03:57.036 --> 00:03:59.505
That is such
a classic old-man move.

00:03:59.505 --> 00:04:02.841
"Grandpa, you can't park there."
"But it's empty."

00:04:02.841 --> 00:04:06.511
"It's a sidewalk!"
"I don't care!"

00:04:06.511 --> 00:04:07.780
What all this makes clear

00:04:07.780 --> 00:04:09.749
is that the GOP's
immigration rhetoric

00:04:09.749 --> 00:04:11.984
was never about
respect for the rule of law.

00:04:11.984 --> 00:04:13.519
It was about
punishing immigrants.

00:04:13.519 --> 00:04:15.555
And that was on display
yet again in yesterday's

00:04:15.555 --> 00:04:17.957
surreal meeting with Democratic
leaders in the Oval Office

00:04:17.957 --> 00:04:20.526
where the President threatened
to shut down the government

00:04:20.526 --> 00:04:22.495
unless he gets funding
for his border wall.

00:04:22.495 --> 00:04:24.597
Watch him bicker
with Democratic leaders

00:04:24.597 --> 00:04:27.566
Chuck Schumer and Nancy Pelosi,
who successfully bait him

00:04:27.566 --> 00:04:30.703
into admitting that he actually
wants a government shutdown.

00:04:30.703 --> 00:04:32.939
-I think the
American people recognize

00:04:32.939 --> 00:04:35.408
that we must keep
government open,

00:04:35.408 --> 00:04:37.877
that a shutdown
is not worth anything

00:04:37.877 --> 00:04:40.913
and that we should not have
a Trump shutdown.

00:04:40.913 --> 00:04:43.982
-You said Trump --

00:04:43.982 --> 00:04:46.886
-You have the White House,
you have the Senate.

00:04:46.886 --> 00:04:48.720
-The one thing
I think we can agree on

00:04:48.720 --> 00:04:51.256
is we shouldn't shut down
the government over a dispute.

00:04:51.256 --> 00:04:53.960
And you want to shut it down.
You keep talking about it.

00:04:53.960 --> 00:04:55.895
-The last time, Chuck,
you shut it down.

00:04:55.895 --> 00:04:57.029
-No, no, no.

00:04:57.029 --> 00:04:58.531
-And then you opened it
very quickly.

00:04:58.531 --> 00:04:59.765
I don't want to do what you did.

00:04:59.765 --> 00:05:01.534
-20 times,
you have called for --

00:05:01.534 --> 00:05:04.069
"I will shut down the government
if I don't get my wall."

00:05:04.069 --> 00:05:05.772
None of us have said --
-You want to know something?

00:05:05.772 --> 00:05:07.039
-You've said it.

00:05:07.039 --> 00:05:08.174
-You want to put that on my --
I'll take it.

00:05:08.174 --> 00:05:10.242
-Okay. Good.
-You know what I'll say?

00:05:10.242 --> 00:05:13.612
Yes, if we don't get what
we want, one way or the other,

00:05:13.612 --> 00:05:15.948
whether it's through you,
through our military,

00:05:15.948 --> 00:05:17.717
through anything
you want to call,

00:05:17.717 --> 00:05:20.186
I will shut down the government.
-Okay. Fair enough.

00:05:20.186 --> 00:05:21.654
We disagree.
-And I'll tell you what.

00:05:21.654 --> 00:05:24.157
I am proud to shut down
the government

00:05:24.157 --> 00:05:25.725
for border security, Chuck.

00:05:25.725 --> 00:05:29.094
-Look how happy Chuck Schumer is

00:05:29.094 --> 00:05:31.097
that he got
Donald Trump to admit.

00:05:31.097 --> 00:05:34.867
That's how he looks when he sees
a sign that says "free soup."

00:05:34.867 --> 00:05:36.769
[ Laughter ]

00:05:36.769 --> 00:05:39.038
Pelosi then reminded Trump
that until January

00:05:39.038 --> 00:05:41.841
Republicans still control all
three branches of government

00:05:41.841 --> 00:05:44.209
and could easily pass
a government funding bill

00:05:44.209 --> 00:05:45.978
on their own,
and Trump responded

00:05:45.978 --> 00:05:48.247
by trying to teach Pelosi
how Congress works.

00:05:48.247 --> 00:05:50.316
-You have the votes,
you should pass it.

00:05:50.316 --> 00:05:52.218
-No, we don't have the votes,
Nancy, because in the Senate

00:05:52.218 --> 00:05:53.619
we need 60 votes,
and we don't have it.

00:05:53.619 --> 00:05:55.555
-No, no, but in the House.
You could bring it up right now.

00:05:55.555 --> 00:05:56.888
-Yeah, but I can't -- Excuse me.

00:05:56.888 --> 00:05:59.592
The House we could get it passed
very easily, and we do,

00:05:59.592 --> 00:06:01.227
but the problem is the Senate

00:06:01.227 --> 00:06:03.462
because we need
10 Democrats to vote.

00:06:03.462 --> 00:06:05.230
Nancy, I'd have it passed
in two seconds.

00:06:05.230 --> 00:06:06.432
It doesn't matter, though,

00:06:06.432 --> 00:06:08.167
because we can't get it passed
in the Senate

00:06:08.167 --> 00:06:09.969
because we need
10 Democrat votes.

00:06:09.969 --> 00:06:12.004
And the House would give me
the vote if I wanted it,

00:06:12.004 --> 00:06:13.405
but I can't because I need --

00:06:13.405 --> 00:06:15.641
Nancy, I need
10 votes from Chuck.

00:06:15.641 --> 00:06:17.242
-I'm sorry.
Are you explaining

00:06:17.242 --> 00:06:21.113
how legislation works
to Nancy Pelosi?

00:06:21.113 --> 00:06:25.084
You might as well try explaining
basketball to LeBron James.

00:06:25.084 --> 00:06:27.954
"And if you stand
behind this line,

00:06:27.954 --> 00:06:30.122
it counts as 3 points, LeBaron."

00:06:30.122 --> 00:06:32.257
Of course if you don't
want to say something stupid,

00:06:32.257 --> 00:06:34.226
the other option is to not
say anything at all,

00:06:34.226 --> 00:06:36.495
and that's the strategy
Vice President Mike Pence chose.

00:06:36.495 --> 00:06:42.367
I mean, look at how still
he was during this meeting.

00:06:42.367 --> 00:06:45.604
He looks like a grandpa
staring off in the distance

00:06:45.604 --> 00:06:46.973
while his children fight

00:06:46.973 --> 00:06:50.576
over whether to put him
in a nursing home.

00:06:50.576 --> 00:06:53.945
[Grumbling]

00:06:53.945 --> 00:06:58.217
"Uh...I want to stay.

00:06:58.217 --> 00:07:01.053
I want to say in my..."
[ Laughs ]

00:07:01.053 --> 00:07:04.257
Every few minutes,
he'd shoot out of his chair

00:07:04.257 --> 00:07:06.158
and have a flashback to Vietnam.

00:07:06.158 --> 00:07:08.527
"They're in the trees!"

00:07:08.527 --> 00:07:10.696
He barely moved!

00:07:10.696 --> 00:07:13.399
Is that the real Mike Pence
or did he pull a Ferris Bueller

00:07:13.399 --> 00:07:17.069
and put a mannequin in his place
that looks exactly like --

00:07:17.069 --> 00:07:18.570
During that meeting,
the real Mike Pence

00:07:18.570 --> 00:07:22.341
was driving a Ferrari to a Cubs
game and singing in a parade.

00:07:22.341 --> 00:07:24.176
[ Laughter ]

00:07:24.176 --> 00:07:25.644
Even Nancy Pelosi,

00:07:25.644 --> 00:07:27.547
who has been in professional
politics for decades,

00:07:27.547 --> 00:07:30.316
had to admit that arguing with
Trump in front of the TV cameras

00:07:30.316 --> 00:07:32.751
was one of the most surreal
experiences of her career.

00:07:32.751 --> 00:07:34.853
And her description of the
meeting kept getting weirder.

00:07:34.853 --> 00:07:37.322
For example, she later described
to her Democratic colleagues

00:07:37.322 --> 00:07:39.826
what Trump said in private
once the cameras were off.

00:07:39.826 --> 00:07:41.594
"He said at the end
of the meeting,

00:07:41.594 --> 00:07:43.662
'We can go two routes
with this meeting --

00:07:43.662 --> 00:07:47.266
with a knife or with a candy.'"

00:07:47.266 --> 00:07:49.135
Why is he so weird?

00:07:49.135 --> 00:07:52.004
[ Laughter ]

00:07:52.004 --> 00:07:56.275
Knife and candy aren't
the two ways to have a meeting.

00:07:56.275 --> 00:07:59.712
They're the two ways
to get somebody into a van.

00:07:59.712 --> 00:08:01.780
[ Laughter ]

00:08:01.780 --> 00:08:04.283
It's like "Head Injuries
Untouchables."

00:08:04.283 --> 00:08:08.153
"They bring a knife,
you bring a candy.

00:08:08.153 --> 00:08:11.457
That's the Dum Dum way."

00:08:11.457 --> 00:08:14.193
What all this makes clear is
the GOP's immigration rhetoric

00:08:14.193 --> 00:08:16.262
was never about respect
or the rule of law.

00:08:16.262 --> 00:08:18.263
All they want
is their stupid border wall,

00:08:18.263 --> 00:08:19.965
and they want us to pay for it.

00:08:19.965 --> 00:08:21.934
And Democrats are responding
by saying...

00:08:21.934 --> 00:08:23.535
-I don't care.

00:08:23.535 --> 00:08:25.872
-This has been "A Closer Look."

